    "properties": {
      "title": "Amazon dams and waterfalls used to assess fish access to suitable habitat",
      "description": "Dams can block fish from reaching suitable habitat as the climate changes. A study combining fish-distribution models with river connectivity found that the Amazon–Solimões corridor retains extensive connected, suitable habitat, while planned hydropower expansion and climate change could reduce such areas. This layer provides the dam and waterfall locations used to examine those risks and supports inspection of barriers relevant to energy and river-conservation planning. It contains current barriers and additional future-scenario records. The points are study inputs: the modeled habitat-access results and dam-impact rankings are not included in this layer.",
