    "properties": {
      "title": "Tropical forest biomass vulnerability to climate and land-use pressures",
      "description": "Satellite observations show that tropical forests respond differently to climate and land-use pressures. The study found widespread vulnerability in the Americas and slower recovery of forest carbon cycling as stress increased. This map shows the biomass component of that assessment, helping identify regions for closer monitoring and conservation or restoration planning. Negative index values indicate vulnerability toward biomass loss, positive values toward higher biomass, and values near zero relative stability. It is a standardized diagnostic index based on observed relationships; it does not measure carbon stocks, predict a probability of collapse, or estimate the benefit of a restoration intervention.",
